# PANopt Zellij Plugin: Pane Spawning & Reconcile Loop Architecture

## Overview

The PANopt sidebar plugin (wasm32-wasip1) consists of:
- **panopt-zellij** (/home/gregz/cp/panopt/crates/panopt-zellij/src/main.rs): The Zellij plugin shell, handles I/O with Zellij's host ABI
- **panopt-zellij-logic** (/home/gregz/cp/panopt/crates/panopt-zellij-logic/src/lib.rs): Transport-free projection parsers, filter/sort logic, pure testable code

---

## 1. How the Plugin Creates Panes: Command Construction

### Agent/Claude-code Pane Today

**Location**: `/home/gregz/cp/panopt/crates/panopt-zellij/src/main.rs:2000-2022` — `spawn_agent_pane()`

The plugin constructs and launches agent panes as follows:

```rust
fn spawn_agent_pane(&mut self, id: Option<&str>) {
    let (final_id, label) = match id {
        Some(given) => (given.to_string(), given.to_string()),
        None => {
            self.next_agent += 1;
            let n = self.next_agent;
            (format!("cockpit-agent-{n}"), format!("Agent {n}"))
        }
    };
    let args = vec!["_agent".to_string(), "--id".to_string(), final_id.clone()];
    let Some(PaneId::Terminal(tid)) = self.spawn_in_slot(args, true) else {
        return;
    };
    self.agent_labels.insert(tid, label);
    self.agent_pane_ids.insert(tid, final_id);
    write_agent_labels(&self.agent_labels);
}
```

**Exact command built for a spawned agent pane** (via `spawn_in_slot` at line 1930-1951):

```rust
fn spawn_in_slot(&mut self, args: Vec<String>, focus: bool) -> Option<PaneId> {
    let ws = self.launch_cwd()?;  // Get project workspace root
    let command = CommandToRun {
        path: PathBuf::from(&self.panopt_bin),  // e.g. "/path/to/panopt"
        args,                                    // e.g. vec!["_agent", "--id", "cockpit-agent-1"]
        cwd: Some(ws),                          // Project root (from layout config `ws`)
    };
    let new = match self.slot_pane {
        Some(slot) => {
            open_command_pane_in_place_of_pane_id(slot, command, false, BTreeMap::new())
        }
        None => open_command_pane(command, BTreeMap::new()),
    };
    // ... store pane id
    new
}
```

**Full command as passed to Zellij**:
